PC menu, HUD placement, FPS readout, and shortcut labels.
Desktop = no touch and innerWidth > 1024. Mobile path was not restyled.

node --check world/input.js world/hud.js world/icon-garage.js : pass

Headless Chrome (one browser), world.html:

1920x1080 hasTouch false
  pc-mode, 15 game cards inside the pause panel (scroll 422 / client 422, panel inside the window)
  START button inside the start card
  shortcuts: THROTTLE [W / ↑], BRAKE [S / ↓], NOS [SHIFT], WINGS [F · G MODE], EXIT [C], ENTER BUILDING [E], pause [ESC]
  keys: G arcade->street, W sets throttle and streetThrottle, S sets brake only, Space sets e-brake only and releases it, Esc and P toggle pause
  AIR/BRAKE label swap keeps [S / ↓]
  on foot: WALK [W / ↑], RUN [SHIFT + W], JUMP [SPACE], ENTER [C], EMOTE [1-4], digit 1 fires emote up
  no button overlap among brake, nos, wings, throttle, fps, pause, exit, enter

1366x768, 1536x864, 1280x720
  same: 15 cards fully inside the panel, START visible, shortcuts present, no overlap

844x390 hasTouch true, deviceScaleFactor 2
  pc-mode false, pc-key count 0, no #pcFps
  canvas buffer W=844 H=390 (phone sizing, not the desktop cap)
  WINGS still placed by the phone path (inline top)
  button text BRAKE / NOS HOLD with no shortcut footer

jr.html?kmenu=1 and index.html?kmenu=1 at 1366x768
  pc-mode, 15 main-menu tiles, none outside the viewport
  grid scrollHeight equals clientHeight (693)

Headless frame time is tens of ms, so the live readout showed about 22 FPS. The node is the real smoothed counter (N FPS).
